Do not build the standalone vtkpython / pvtkpython interpreter executables when
VTK_INSTALL_PYTHON_EXES is OFF.

The vtk-python-cp312 package ships ONLY the Python wrapper artifacts (the
libvtk*Python archives, _vtkmodules_static.a, _vtk.zip and the vtkmodules
package + headers) and never the standalone `vtkpython` CLI — the recipe already
sets VTK_INSTALL_PYTHON_EXES=OFF so it is not installed, and the prune step drops
it regardless. Upstream still *builds* the executable (it is only gated on
NOT VTK_WHEEL_BUILD), and on the static wasm / wasm-mt build that fat final link
(every wrapped module + libpython3.12.a) fails anyway:
  * libpython3.12.a(_decimal.o) references mpd_isspecial (libmpdecimal is not
    archived into the wasm CPython), and (sha2module.o) references
    python_hashlib_Hacl_Hash_SHA2_* (the HACL SHA2 objects are not archived);
  * on wasm-mt the threaded link adds --no-growable-memory --initial-memory=16MiB
    and the executable's static data exceeds it ("initial memory too small").
Building an executable we never ship, only to have it fail and be tolerated by
`ninja -k 0`, wastes the single heaviest link+wasm-opt step of the build and — on
the heavier wasm-mt cell — tips the job over. Gate the whole interpreter block on
VTK_INSTALL_PYTHON_EXES so it is skipped entirely when we are not installing it.
Nothing depends on the vtkpython target (only VTK_BUILD_TESTING, OFF here); the
_vtk.zip / _vtkmodules_static.a / wrapper archives are produced independently.

No-op on native platforms: VTK_INSTALL_PYTHON_EXES defaults ON there (the native
build.sh/build.ps1 do not set it), so `NOT VTK_WHEEL_BUILD AND
VTK_INSTALL_PYTHON_EXES` stays TRUE and the executables build exactly as before.
--- a/Wrapping/Python/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Wrapping/Python/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -22,7 +22,12 @@ endif ()
 endif ()

 # The interpreters are not supported in wheel builds, so skip them.
-if (NOT VTK_WHEEL_BUILD)
+# cvcpkg: also skip when VTK_INSTALL_PYTHON_EXES is OFF — the vtk-python-cp312
+# package ships only the wrapper archives / _vtkmodules_static.a / _vtk.zip and
+# never the standalone vtkpython, whose fat static link fails on wasm anyway
+# (mpd_isspecial + HACL SHA2 undefs, and on wasm-mt the threaded
+# --no-growable-memory 16 MiB initial-memory cap). Nothing depends on the target.
+if (NOT VTK_WHEEL_BUILD AND VTK_INSTALL_PYTHON_EXES)
   add_executable(vtkpython)
   target_sources(vtkpython
     PRIVATE
